      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "By finding the missing values in the ratio table below, determine which of the following graphs represents the given relationship.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $4$ |\n|  | $8$ |\n| $15$ |  |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $5:4$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\times 2}{4\\times 2} & =\\frac{10}{8} \\\\ \\frac{5\\times 3}{4\\times 3} & =\\frac{15}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $4$ |\n| $10$ | $8$ |\n| $15$ | $12$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following ordered pairs: $(5,4),$ $(10,8),$ $(15,12).$\n\nPlotting these points on the coordinate plane, we get:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152648/assets/d4bf54ac87bed89a5384359136feb1e5e0e090f6f7065b48ea99915f4fafdfb0.png)",
